## 🗺️ Phased Implementation Roadmap

### Phase 1 — Core Pipeline ✅ *(Current)*

| Component | Status | Description |
|-----------|--------|-------------|
| `validator.py` | ✅ Done | Regex-based GitHub URL parser (HTTPS, SSH, API formats) |
| `github_fetcher.py` | ✅ Done | Fetches repo tree + file contents via GitHub API, fully in-memory |
| `separator.py` | ✅ Done | `process_repo()` walks filesystem; categorizes by extension/name |
| `chunker.py` | 🟡 Needs Fix | Structure-aware + token-budget chunking; has a logic bug in `chunk_file` |
| `main.py` | 🔄 Wiring | Currently minimal — needs to connect fetcher → separator → chunker |

**Goals for Phase 1:**
```
input:  GitHub URL
output: {
  "owner", "repo", "branch",
  "total_files_fetched": N,
  "categories": { code, config, docs, binary, other },
  "total_chunks": N
}
```

### Phase 2 — Repo-Scoped Q&A 🎯 *(Next)*

| Component | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Scope Enforcer** | Build a context window that only includes chunks from the target repo + dependency metadata |
| **Dependency Parser** | Parse `requirements.txt`, `package.json`, `go.mod`, `Cargo.toml` etc. to know what libraries the repo uses |
| **LLM Orchestrator** | Send chunk-grounded queries to an LLM with strict system prompts banning out-of-scope answers |
| **Query Router** | `POST /query` endpoint that accepts a question and returns a repo-grounded answer |

**Key constraint:**
```python
# Pseudocode for the scoping rule
ALLOWED_SOURCES = repo_chunks + dependency_metadata
if any(source not in ALLOWED_SOURCES for source in llm_response_sources):
    reject("Answer references content outside the repository")
```

### Phase 3 — TUI (Terminal User Interface) 🖥️ *(Future)*

| Component | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Textual App** | Rich terminal UI using [Textual](https://textual.textualize.io/) |
| **Repo Explorer** | Navigable tree view of repo files with category badges |
| **Chunk Viewer** | Browse individual chunks with token counts and strategy labels |
| **Q&A Panel** | Ask questions inline, see answers with source-file citations |
| **Session History** | Persist analysis sessions locally for later review |

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Repo Ranger                                     [X]    │
├────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┤
│  📁 repo structure     │  💬 Q&A Panel                  │
│                        │                                 │
│  src/                  │  Q: Why is this function async? │
│   ├─ main.py          │                                 │
│   ├─ utils/           │  A: From utils/fetcher.py:47    │
│   │  └─ fetcher.py    │  The API client uses asyncio    │
│   └─ models.py        │  to handle concurrent requests. │
│                        │                                 │
│  tests/                │                                 │
│   └─ test_main.py     │                                 │
│                        │                                 │
│  [code] [config] [docs]│  [Ask a question...]          │
├────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┤
│  Stats: 142 files · 1,234 chunks · 45,678 tokens        │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 🔮 Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|----------|-----------|
| **No `git clone`** | Avoids disk I/O, works in serverless/constrained environments, faster startup |
| **In-memory pipeline** | Simpler state management, easy to parallelize, no cleanup needed |
| **tiktoken for budgeting** | Industry-standard tokenization matching OpenAI models; predictable chunk sizes |
| **AST-based Python chunking** | Preserves function/class boundaries instead of arbitrary splits |
| **FastAPI over Flask** | Native async support, auto-docs, Pydantic integration out of the box |

---

## 🧪 Potential Issues & Mitigations

| Issue | Risk | Mitigation |
|-------|------|------------|
| **GitHub API rate limits** | High | Support tokens via header; cache results per session |
| **Large repos (>300k entries)** | Medium | Tree endpoint truncates — need pagination or shallow-first strategy |
| **Binary file detection** | Low | Currently extension-based; could add magic byte sniffing |
| **Token costs for large repos** | Medium | Allow user to filter by category (e.g., "code only") |
| **LLM context window overflow** | Medium | Implement retrieval (RAG) over chunks instead of dumping all |
| **Chunker bug (dead code path)** | Low | `chunk_file` has unreachable branches — needs refactor |
